      "content": "Take a breath — this is only a 1-mark idiom question, so you do not need a long essay. An idiom is not meant literally: 'raising the roof' paints a picture of people being so loud and excited that the roof seems to lift. In this advert it pushes the idea of making a public noise about homeless youth, not actually lifting a building. Before I confirm the exact wording: what do you think people are doing at a concert or party when they 'raise the roof'?"
